1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,790
A client chooses this jacket.

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,260
A similar jacket is not the same choice.

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,520
How do you keep that decision connected to the item that gets
packed?

4
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:13,101
ClosetRelay connects a client's choice to one physical item.

5
00:00:13,101 --> 00:00:17,228
Here, fictional appointments use the working local application.

6
00:00:17,228 --> 00:00:21,290
Record the selected navy jacket, then place an exclusive hold.

7
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:27,701
Update the item's condition before packing, and the old approval
and hold no longer apply.

8
00:00:27,701 --> 00:00:30,526
Review the changed record and approve it again.

9
00:00:30,526 --> 00:00:33,291
An old decision cannot silently carry forward.

10
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:36,062
Let's scan the other jacket.

11
00:00:36,062 --> 00:00:37,454
The server rejects it.

12
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:41,250
The correct jacket stays held, and nothing is marked packed.

13
00:00:42,251 --> 00:00:44,217
Scan the exact item instead.

14
00:00:44,217 --> 00:00:46,464
One packing handoff is recorded.

15
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:52,011
Reloading preserves it, and another appointment cannot approve
the packed item.

16
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:58,771
The YouCam preview panel is designed to bind an image to that
same item and consent revision.

17
00:00:58,771 --> 00:01:03,292
Live YouCam is not connected here; this video claims no
generated result.

18
00:01:04,292 --> 00:01:06,617
This is one local operator workflow.

19
00:01:06,617 --> 00:01:13,852
Separate client logins, real provider validation, and comparison
with existing styling tools are still required.

20
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:15,985
ClosetRelay.

21
00:01:15,985 --> 00:01:17,465
The chosen item.

22
00:01:17,465 --> 00:01:18,760
The held item.

23
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,240
The packed item.

24
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,275
One continuous record.
